    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a visualiser is published",
      "prov:value": "Owner,\n2026-10-05 (issue #2188, PR #2189, bean `kc7k`): the pages authored in\ncat-harness's `docs/` folder publish under `<base>/docs/cat-harness/` —\n`concepts/architecture.md` → `<base>/docs/cat-harness/concepts/architecture.html`,\nits locale copy at `<base>/docs/cat-harness/concepts/fr/architecture.html` —\nwith no redirects at the old addresses. Nothing else moved: the landing page\n`<base>/` and each locale landing `<base>/fr/`, the instance sites (case 2),\nthe viewers (case 3), the kind directories the same tree publishes\n(`<base>/processes/`, `<base>/proposals/` …) and every root export keep their\nURLs.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean kc7k",
        "#2188",
        "#2189",
        "2026-10-05",
        "PR 2189"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Serialisations — the obligation that cannot be waived",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-09-20, in two rulings that belong together:\n\n> all dir urls should have json, jsonld, schema.json like\n> `<base-url>/beans.jsonld`",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this one takes no `exempt`",
      "prov:value": "A harness that\ncould waive it could declare a directory into the knowledge graph and then make\nits contents unreachable — which is the `dh4f` defect with a signature on it, a\nconsumer scanning nothing and reporting a clean run over it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this one takes no `exempt`",
      "prov:value": "`SubgraphCoverageSchema.exempt` carries three keys and not four, and\n`tsc` enforces it — adding `serialisations` to `CRITERIA` turned the checker's\nwaiver lookup into a type error rather than a silent `undefined` that would\nhave read as \"not exempted\" and worked by luck."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "How it fits the render pipeline",
      "prov:value": "The pipeline the sibling branches are converging on is four parts per graph —\n**reader → projection → viewer → gate** (PR #583 for `schemas/` and `library/`,\nthis branch for the state graphs).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#583",
        "PR 583"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "How it fits the render pipeline",
      "prov:value": "**Do not compose these URLs by hand.** `o7eq` records that hand-composition\nproduced four incompatible URL shapes across four open branches on a single\nday."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you declare a directory",
      "prov:value": "A directory whose nodes are not addressable has not entered the graph.\n2. **Declare only what exists.** A declared-but-absent directory is the `dh4f`\n   defect: a consumer scans nothing and reports a clean run over it.\n3."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading the axis",
      "prov:value": "That is not softness:\n0 of 20 non-content directories have a declared visualiser today, and a hard\ngate on day one is a wall somebody switches off."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reading the axis",
      "prov:value": "- **Never quote a count from prose.** The numbers in this file are from\n  2026-09-20 and are provenance for the rules, not a description of today.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "See also",
      "prov:value": "- [`directory-conventions`](directory-conventions.md) — the declaration schema\n  and every graph typology\n- [`content-context-and-state-graphs`](content-context-and-state-graphs.md) —\n  what `holds` means, and the one question that settles a kind\n- [`kg-viewer`](../../ui/ui-core/kg-viewer.md) — the viewer this repository already ships\n- `bun run cat check:subgraph-coverage` — the axis; `schemas/kg/cat-harness.ts`\n  `owesVisualiser()` — the visualiser obligation, and\n  `SubgraphCoverageSchema.serialisations` — the one that takes no waiver\n- `url-space` — bean `o7eq` (`beans show folio-assistant-o7eq`) for where a\n  rendered asset is addressed, and why not to compose that URL by hand",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean o7eq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/harness-requirements.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Serialisations — the obligation that cannot be waived",
      "prov:value": "> also subpaths must remain addressable… like `<base-url>/beans/bean-id.jsonld`,\n> json and schema etc if there, harnesses cannot override there being in the KG",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
